  "cash_ledger_join": "Design 2.1:75 and 13:376 - each fee_events row is the typed projection of exactly one fee-kind cash_events row joined by cash_event_id, and the typed signed delta equals the joined cash signed delta. fee_events/0.fee_cash_delta = -0.1 = cash_events/0.signed_delta (CE-FEE-0); fee_events/1.fee_cash_delta = -0.1 = cash_events/1.signed_delta (CE-FEE-1). Gross realization appears only in cash_events (CE-GROSS-1). The M-06 observation window is the full bar span 2000-01-01T00:10:00Z..2000-01-01T00:12:00Z, so only the three cash_events rows are applied to equity: 1000 + (-0.1) + (-0.1) + 0 = 999.8.",
  "time_stop_derivation": "Design 22.6:886 binds the bar series [INIT98, ENTRY100, (2000-01-01T00:12:00Z, 2, 100, 100, 100, 100, 0)] with use_time_stop = true, time_stop_bars = 1, time_stop_condition = 'Always'. The real entry fills at 100 on ENTRY100 (fallback_notional 1000 * 10% = 100 over reference 100 gives quantity 1), and the time stop closes quantity 1 at 100 on the next bar. The corrected event class, exit id and reason are the design-stated MARKET_EXIT / TIME_STOP / time_stop, and lifecycle ids start at 1. RULE2-07 keeps its stated taker rate 0.001 (design 22.3:802).",
